Table full name: bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_acs.censustract_2017_5yr
Column name: geo_id Type: STRING Description: US Census Tracts Geoids
Column name: nonfamily_households Type: FLOAT64 Description: Nonfamily Households. A householder living alone or with nonrelatives only. Unmarried couples households, whether opposite-sex or same-sex, with no relatives of the householder present are tabulated in nonfamily households.
Column name: family_households Type: FLOAT64 Description: Family Households. A family consists of a householder and one or more other people living in the same household who are related to the householder by birth, marriage, or adoption. All people in a household who are related to the householder are regarded as members of his or her family. A family household may contain people not related to the householder, but those people are not included as part of the family of the householder in tabulations. Thus, the number of family households is equal to the number of families, but family households may include more members than do families. A household can contain only one family for purposes of tabulations. Not all households contain families since a household may be comprised of a group of unrelated people or of one person living alone -- these are called nonfamily households. Families are classified by type as either a "married couple family" or "other family" according to the sex of the householder and the presence of relatives. The data on family type are based ...
Column name: median_year_structure_built Type: FLOAT64 Description: Median Year Structure Built. Median Year Structure Built
Column name: rent_burden_not_computed Type: FLOAT64 Description: Housing units without rent burden computed. Units for which no rent is paid and units occupied by households that reported no income or a net loss comprise this category
Column name: rent_over_50_percent Type: FLOAT64 Description: Housing units spending over 50% income on rent. Gross rent over 50 percent of household income. Computed ratio of monthly gross rent to monthly household income (total household income divided by 12). The ratio is computed separately for each unit and is rounded to the nearest tenth. Units for which no rent is paid and units occupied by households that report no income or a net loss comprise the category, "Not computed". Gross rent as a percentage of household income provides information on the monthly housing cost expenses for renters. 
Column name: rent_40_to_50_percent Type: FLOAT64 Description: Housing units spending 40 to 49.9% income on rent. Gross rent from 40.0 to 49.9 percent of household income. Computed ratio of monthly gross rent to monthly household income (total household income divided by 12). The ratio is computed separately for each unit and is rounded to the nearest tenth. Units for which no rent is paid and units occupied by households that report no income or a net loss comprise the category, "Not computed". Gross rent as a percentage of household income provides information on the monthly housing cost expenses for renters. 
Column name: rent_35_to_40_percent Type: FLOAT64 Description: Housing units spending 35 to 39.9% income on rent. Gross rent from 35.0 to 39.9 percent of household income. Computed ratio of monthly gross rent to monthly household income (total household income divided by 12). The ratio is computed separately for each unit and is rounded to the nearest tenth. Units for which no rent is paid and units occupied by households that report no income or a net loss comprise the category, "Not computed". Gross rent as a percentage of household income provides information on the monthly housing cost expenses for renters. 
Column name: rent_30_to_35_percent Type: FLOAT64 Description: Housing units spending 30 to 34.9% income on rent. Gross rent from 30.0 to 34.9 percent of household income. Computed ratio of monthly gross rent to monthly household income (total household income divided by 12). The ratio is computed separately for each unit and is rounded to the nearest tenth. Units for which no rent is paid and units occupied by households that report no income or a net loss comprise the category, "Not computed". Gross rent as a percentage of household income provides information on the monthly housing cost expenses for renters. 
Column name: rent_25_to_30_percent Type: FLOAT64 Description: Housing units spending 25 to 29.9% income on rent. Gross rent from 25.0 to 29.9 percent of household income. Computed ratio of monthly gross rent to monthly household income (total household income divided by 12). The ratio is computed separately for each unit and is rounded to the nearest tenth. Units for which no rent is paid and units occupied by households that report no income or a net loss comprise the category, "Not computed". Gross rent as a percentage of household income provides information on the monthly housing cost expenses for renters. 
Column name: rent_20_to_25_percent Type: FLOAT64 Description: Housing units spending 20 to 24.9% income on rent. Gross rent from 20.0 to 24.9 percent of household income. Computed ratio of monthly gross rent to monthly household income (total household income divided by 12). The ratio is computed separately for each unit and is rounded to the nearest tenth. Units for which no rent is paid and units occupied by households that report no income or a net loss comprise the category, "Not computed". Gross rent as a percentage of household income provides information on the monthly housing cost expenses for renters. 
Column name: rent_15_to_20_percent Type: FLOAT64 Description: Housing units spending 15 to 19.9% income on rent. Gross rent from 15.0 to 19.9 percent of household income. Computed ratio of monthly gross rent to monthly household income (total household income divided by 12). The ratio is computed separately for each unit and is rounded to the nearest tenth. Units for which no rent is paid and units occupied by households that report no income or a net loss comprise the category, "Not computed". Gross rent as a percentage of household income provides information on the monthly housing cost expenses for renters. 
Column name: rent_10_to_15_percent Type: FLOAT64 Description: Housing units spending 10 to 14.9% income on rent. Gross rent from 10.0 to 14.9 percent of household income. Computed ratio of monthly gross rent to monthly household income (total household income divided by 12). The ratio is computed separately for each unit and is rounded to the nearest tenth. Units for which no rent is paid and units occupied by households that report no income or a net loss comprise the category, "Not computed". Gross rent as a percentage of household income provides information on the monthly housing cost expenses for renters. 
Column name: rent_under_10_percent Type: FLOAT64 Description: Housing units spending less than 10% on rent. Gross rent less than 10 percent of household income. Computed ratio of monthly gross rent to monthly household income (total household income divided by 12). The ratio is computed separately for each unit and is rounded to the nearest tenth. Units for which no rent is paid and units occupied by households that report no income or a net loss comprise the category, "Not computed". Gross rent as a percentage of household income provides information on the monthly housing cost expenses for renters. 
Column name: total_pop Type: FLOAT64 Description: Total Population. The total number of all people living in a given geographic area.  This is a very useful catch-all denominator when calculating rates.
Column name: male_pop Type: FLOAT64 Description: Male Population. The number of people within each geography who are male.
Column name: female_pop Type: FLOAT64 Description: Female Population. The number of people within each geography who are female.
Column name: median_age Type: FLOAT64 Description: Median Age. The median age of all people in a given geographic area.
Column name: white_pop Type: FLOAT64 Description: White Population. The number of people identifying as white, non-Hispanic in each geography.
Column name: black_pop Type: FLOAT64 Description: Black or African American Population. The number of people identifying as black or African American, non-Hispanic in each geography.
Column name: asian_pop Type: FLOAT64 Description: Asian Population. The number of people identifying as Asian, non-Hispanic in each geography.
Column name: hispanic_pop Type: FLOAT64 Description: Hispanic Population. The number of people identifying as Hispanic or Latino in each geography.
Column name: amerindian_pop Type: FLOAT64 Description: American Indian and Alaska Native Population. The number of people identifying as American Indian or Alaska native in each geography.
Column name: other_race_pop Type: FLOAT64 Description: Other Race population. The number of people identifying as another race in each geography
Column name: two_or_more_races_pop Type: FLOAT64 Description: Two or more races population. The number of people identifying as two or more races in each geography
Column name: not_hispanic_pop Type: FLOAT64 Description: Population not Hispanic. The number of people not identifying as Hispanic or Latino in each geography.
Column name: commuters_by_public_transportation Type: FLOAT64 Description: Commuters by Public Transportation. The number of workers age 16 years and over within a geographic area who primarily traveled to work by public transportation.  This is the principal mode of travel or type of conveyance, by distance rather than time, that the worker usually used to get from home to work.
Column name: households Type: FLOAT64 Description: Households. A count of the number of households in each geography. A household consists of one or more people who live in the same dwelling and also share at meals or living accommodation, and may consist of a single family or some other grouping of people. 
Column name: median_income Type: FLOAT64 Description: Median Household Income in the past 12 Months. Within a geographic area, the median income received by every household on a regular basis before payments for personal income taxes, social security, union dues, medicare deductions, etc.  It includes income received from wages, salary, commissions, bonuses, and tips; self-employment income from own nonfarm or farm businesses, including proprietorships and partnerships; interest, dividends, net rental income, royalty income, or income from estates and trusts; Social Security or Railroad Retirement income; Supplemental Security Income (SSI); any cash public assistance or welfare payments from the state or local welfare office; retirement, survivor, or disability benefits; and any other sources of income received regularly such as Veterans' (VA) payments, unemployment and/or worker's compensation, child support, and alimony.
Column name: income_per_capita Type: FLOAT64 Description: Per Capita Income in the past 12 Months. Per capita income is the mean income computed for every man, woman, and child in a particular group. It is derived by dividing the total income of a particular group by the total population.
Column name: housing_units Type: FLOAT64 Description: Housing Units. A count of housing units in each geography.  A housing unit is a house, an apartment, a mobile home or trailer, a group of rooms, or a single room occupied as separate living quarters, or if vacant, intended for occupancy as separate living quarters.
Column name: vacant_housing_units Type: FLOAT64 Description: Vacant Housing Units. The count of vacant housing units in a geographic area. A housing unit is vacant if no one is living in it at the time of enumeration, unless its occupants are only temporarily absent. Units temporarily occupied at the time of enumeration entirely by people who have a usual residence elsewhere are also classified as vacant.
Column name: vacant_housing_units_for_rent Type: FLOAT64 Description: Vacant Housing Units for Rent. The count of vacant housing units in a geographic area that are for rent. A housing unit is vacant if no one is living in it at the time of enumeration, unless its occupants are only temporarily absent. Units temporarily occupied at the time of enumeration entirely by people who have a usual residence elsewhere are also classified as vacant.
Column name: vacant_housing_units_for_sale Type: FLOAT64 Description: Vacant Housing Units for Sale. The count of vacant housing units in a geographic area that are for sale. A housing unit is vacant if no one is living in it at the time of enumeration, unless its occupants are only temporarily absent. Units temporarily occupied at the time of enumeration entirely by people who have a usual residence elsewhere are also classified as vacant.
Column name: median_rent Type: FLOAT64 Description: Median Rent. The median contract rent within a geographic area. The contract rent is the monthly rent agreed to or contracted for, regardless of any furnishings, utilities, fees, meals, or services that may be included. For vacant units, it is the monthly rent asked for the rental unit at the time of interview.
Column name: percent_income_spent_on_rent Type: FLOAT64 Description: Percent of Household Income Spent on Rent. Within a geographic area, the median percentage of household income which was spent on gross rent.  Gross rent is the amount of the contract rent plus the estimated average monthly cost of utilities (electricity, gas, water, sewer etc.) and fuels (oil, coal, wood, etc.) if these are paid by the renter.  Household income is the sum of the income of all people 15 years and older living in the household.
Column name: owner_occupied_housing_units Type: FLOAT64 Description: Owner-occupied Housing Units
Column name: million_dollar_housing_units Type: FLOAT64 Description: Owner-occupied Housing Units valued at $1,000,000 or more.. The count of owner occupied housing units in a geographic area that are valued at $1,000,000 or more.  Value is the respondent's estimate of how much the property (house and lot, mobile home and lot, or condominium unit) would sell for if it were for sale.
Column name: mortgaged_housing_units Type: FLOAT64 Description: Owner-occupied Housing Units with a Mortgage. The count of housing units within a geographic area that are mortagaged. "Mortgage" refers to all forms of debt where the property is pledged as security for repayment of the debt, including deeds of trust, trust deed, contracts to purchase, land contracts, junior mortgages, and home equity loans.
Column name: families_with_young_children Type: FLOAT64 Description: Families with young children (under 6 years of age)
Column name: two_parent_families_with_young_children Type: FLOAT64 Description: Two-parent families with young children (under 6 years of age)
Column name: two_parents_in_labor_force_families_with_young_children Type: FLOAT64 Description: Two-parent families, both parents in labor force with young children (under 6 years of age)
Column name: two_parents_father_in_labor_force_families_with_young_children Type: FLOAT64 Description: Two-parent families, father only in labor force with young children (under 6 years of age)
Column name: two_parents_mother_in_labor_force_families_with_young_children Type: FLOAT64 Description: Two-parent families, mother only in labor force with young children (under 6 years of age)
Column name: two_parents_not_in_labor_force_families_with_young_children Type: FLOAT64 Description: Two-parent families, neither parent in labor force with young children (under 6 years of age)
Column name: one_parent_families_with_young_children Type: FLOAT64 Description: One-parent families with young children (under 6 years of age)
Column name: father_one_parent_families_with_young_children Type: FLOAT64 Description: One-parent families, father, with young children (under 6 years of age)
Column name: father_in_labor_force_one_parent_families_with_young_children Type: FLOAT64 Description: One-parent families, father in labor force, with young children (under 6 years of age)
Column name: commute_10_14_mins Type: FLOAT64 Description: Number of workers with a commute between 10 and 14 minutes. The number of workers in a geographic area over the age of 16 who do not work from home and commute in between 10 and 14 minutes. 
Column name: commute_15_19_mins Type: FLOAT64 Description: Number of workers with a commute between 15 and 19 minutes. The number of workers in a geographic area over the age of 16 who do not work from home and commute in between 15 and 19 minutes. 
Column name: commute_20_24_mins Type: FLOAT64 Description: Number of workers with a commute between 20 and 24 minutes. The number of workers in a geographic area over the age of 16 who do not work from home and commute in between 20 and 24 minutes.
Column name: commute_25_29_mins Type: FLOAT64 Description: Number of workers with a commute between 25 and 29 minutes. The number of workers in a geographic area over the age of 16 who do not work from home and commute in between 25 and 29 minutes. 
Column name: commute_30_34_mins Type: FLOAT64 Description: Number of workers with a commute between 30 and 34 minutes. The number of workers in a geographic area over the age of 16 who do not work from home and commute in between 30 and 34 minutes. 
Column name: commute_45_59_mins Type: FLOAT64 Description: Number of workers with a commute between 45 and 59 minutes. The number of workers in a geographic area over the age of 16 who do not work from home and commute in between 45 and 59 minutes. 
Column name: aggregate_travel_time_to_work Type: FLOAT64 Description: Aggregate travel time to work. The total number of minutes every worker in a geographic area over the age of 16 who did not work from home spent spent commuting to work in one day
Column name: income_less_10000 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Households with income less than $10,000. The number of households in a geographic area whose annual income was less than $10,000.
Column name: income_10000_14999 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Households with income of $10,000 to $14,999. The number of households in a geographic area whose annual income was between $10,000 and $14,999.
Column name: income_15000_19999 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Households with income of $15,000 to $19,999. The number of households in a geographic area whose annual income was between $15,000 and $19,999.
Column name: income_20000_24999 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Households with income of $20,000 to $24,999. The number of households in a geographic area whose annual income was between $20,000 and $24,999.
Column name: income_25000_29999 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Households with income of $25,000 to $29,999. The number of households in a geographic area whose annual income was between $20,000 and $24,999.
Column name: income_30000_34999 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Households with income of $30,000 to $34,999. The number of households in a geographic area whose annual income was between $30,000 and $34,999.
Column name: income_35000_39999 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Households with income of $35,000 to $39,999. The number of households in a geographic area whose annual income was between $35,000 and $39,999.
Column name: income_40000_44999 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Households with income of $40,000 to $44,999. The number of households in a geographic area whose annual income was between $40,000 and $44,999.
Column name: income_45000_49999 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Households with income of $45,000 to $49,999. The number of households in a geographic area whose annual income was between $45,000 and $49,999.
Column name: income_50000_59999 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Households with income of $50,000 to $59,999. The number of households in a geographic area whose annual income was between $50,000 and $59,999.
Column name: income_60000_74999 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Households with income of $60,000 to $74,999. The number of households in a geographic area whose annual income was between $60,000 and $74,999.
Column name: income_75000_99999 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Households with income of $75,000 to $99,999. The number of households in a geographic area whose annual income was between $75,000 and $99,999.
Column name: income_100000_124999 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Households with income of $100,000 to $124,999. The number of households in a geographic area whose annual income was between $100,000 and $124,999.
Column name: income_125000_149999 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Households with income of $125,000 to $149,999. The number of households in a geographic area whose annual income was between $125,000 and $149,999.
Column name: income_150000_199999 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Households with income of $150,000 to $199,999. The number of households in a geographic area whose annual income was between $150,000 and $1999,999.
Column name: income_200000_or_more Type: FLOAT64 Description: Households with income of $200,000 Or More. The number of households in a geographic area whose annual income was more than $200,000.
Column name: renter_occupied_housing_units_paying_cash_median_gross_rent Type: FLOAT64 Description: Renter-Occupied Housing Units Paying Cash Rent Median Gross Rent
Column name: owner_occupied_housing_units_lower_value_quartile Type: FLOAT64 Description: Owner-Occupied Housing Units Lower Value Quartile
Column name: owner_occupied_housing_units_median_value Type: FLOAT64 Description: Owner-Occupied Housing Units Median Value. The middle value (median) in a geographic area owner occupied housing units.
Column name: owner_occupied_housing_units_upper_value_quartile Type: FLOAT64 Description: Owner-Occupied Housing Units Upper Value Quartile
Column name: married_households Type: FLOAT64 Description: Married households. People in formal marriages, as well as people in common-law marriages, are included. Does not include same-sex marriages.
Column name: occupied_housing_units Type: FLOAT64 Description: Occupied housing units. A housing unit is classified as occupied if it is the usual place of residence of the person or group of people living in it at the time of enumeration.
Column name: housing_units_renter_occupied Type: FLOAT64 Description: Renter occupied housing units. All occupied units which are not owner occupied, whether they are rented for cash rent or occupied without payment of cash rent, are classified as renter-occupied.
Column name: dwellings_1_units_detached Type: FLOAT64 Description: Single-family (one unit) detached dwellings. This is a 1-unit structure detached from any other house, that is, with open space on all four sides. Such structures are considered detached even if they have an adjoining shed or garage. A one-family house that contains a business is considered detached as long as the building has open space on all four sides. Mobile homes to which one or more permanent rooms have been added or built also are included.
Column name: dwellings_1_units_attached Type: FLOAT64 Description: Single-family (one unit) attached dwellings. This is a 1-unit structure that has one or more walls extending from ground to roof separating it from adjoining structures. In row houses (sometimes called townhouses), double houses, or houses attached to nonresidential structures, each house is a separate, attached structure if the dividing or common wall goes from ground to roof.
Column name: dwellings_2_units Type: FLOAT64 Description: Two-family (two unit) dwellings
Column name: dwellings_3_to_4_units Type: FLOAT64 Description: Multifamily dwellings with three to 4 units
Column name: dwellings_5_to_9_units Type: FLOAT64 Description: Apartment buildings with 5 to 9 units
Column name: dwellings_10_to_19_units Type: FLOAT64 Description: Apartment buildings with 10 to 19 units
Column name: dwellings_20_to_49_units Type: FLOAT64 Description: Apartment buildings with 20 to 49 units
Column name: dwellings_50_or_more_units Type: FLOAT64 Description: Apartment buildings with 50 or more units
Column name: mobile_homes Type: FLOAT64 Description: Mobile homes. A manufactured home is defined as a movable dwelling, 8 feet or more wide and 40 feet or more long, designed to be towed on its own chassis, with transportation gear integral to the unit when it leaves the factory, and without need of a permanent foundation. These homes are built in accordance with the U.S. Department of Housing and Urban Development (HUD) building code.
Column name: housing_built_2005_or_later Type: FLOAT64 Description: Housing units built in 2005 or later. A house, an apartment, a mobile home or trailer, a group of rooms, or a single room occupied as separate living quarters, or if vacant, intended for occupancy as separate living quarters built in 2005 or later.
Column name: housing_built_2000_to_2004 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Housing units built between 2000 and 2004. A house, an apartment, a mobile home or trailer, a group of rooms, or a single room occupied as separate living quarters, or if vacant, intended for occupancy as separate living quarters built from 2000 to 2004.
Column name: housing_built_1939_or_earlier Type: FLOAT64 Description: Housing units built before 1939. A house, an apartment, a mobile home or trailer, a group of rooms, or a single room occupied as separate living quarters, or if vacant, intended for occupancy as separate living quarters built in 1939 or earlier.
